WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.740
Do we sell anything that
connects to something?

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:08.460
The Cyber Resilience Act is EU law for
makers of connected hardware and software.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.550
Four questions decide
what it means for us.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.240
First, are we a maker?

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:18.860
The act covers hardware and software
that connects to a device or a network,

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.360
sold in the EU.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.650
Selling under our own name
makes us the manufacturer.

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:25.915
Each product also has a class:

00:00:26.345 --> 00:00:29.115
default, class one, class two or critical.

00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:31.427
Second, the alarm.

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.122
Since 11 September 2026,

00:00:34.552 --> 00:00:40.212
the CRA requires an early warning
within 24 hours of becoming aware that a

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:42.742
vulnerability is actively exploited.

00:00:43.622 --> 00:00:46.292
A notification follows within 72 hours.

00:00:46.642 --> 00:00:51.052
This also covers products we
sold before December 2027.

00:00:51.287 --> 00:00:54.257
Late reporting can be
fined up to 15 million,

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.637
or 2.5 percent of worldwide turnover.

00:00:58.817 --> 00:01:01.667
Third, from 11 December 2027.

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:04.517
Every new product needs
security by design,

00:01:04.927 --> 00:01:08.957
an SBOM, a support period with updates,
and a CE mark.

00:01:09.312 --> 00:01:11.322
Without the mark, no EU market.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.540
Fourth, importers and resellers.

00:01:14.805 --> 00:01:18.415
An importer checks the
manufacturer's file and the CE mark.

00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:22.115
A reseller verifies the mark,
and passes on warnings.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.845
Put our own brand on a product,
and we are the manufacturer.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:28.293
What good looks like.

00:01:28.578 --> 00:01:30.908
One product list, with a class for each.

00:01:31.243 --> 00:01:34.973
A reporting route, with one named
person and a platform account.

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:37.818
An SBOM and a vulnerability process.

00:01:38.773 --> 00:01:40.463
A conformity file for the CE mark.

00:01:40.788 --> 00:01:43.978
The essential requirements
are in Annex One of the act.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.040
A suggested first step.

00:01:47.325 --> 00:01:50.475
Ask for one product list with
a class for each product.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.260
Then rehearse one 24-hour report.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.460
An SBOM and a vulnerability
process are the quickest wins.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.860
The act makes product security

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.180
a condition for selling in the EU.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.510
Know the list, and keep the clock.

